---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy in this preview"
  description="The preview's actual browser data flows and the configuration still needed before public launch."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY BY DESIGN</p>
    <h1>A small data footprint.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This is a development preview notice, not a final commercial privacy
      policy.
    </p>
    <h2>What the browser does</h2>
    <p>
      The application loads HTML, styles, scripts and sample statistical JSON
      from its own origin. It sets no application cookies and uses no analytics,
      advertising pixels, external fonts or account services. Search and filter
      selections appear in the URL, so avoid putting personal information there.
    </p>
    <h2>Network information still exists</h2>
    <p>
      Even a static site sends an IP address and request information to its
      host. Hosting and network providers may process access logs, referrers and
      device details. Production providers, locations, retention settings and a
      privacy contact have not been configured or verified.
    </p>
    <h2>Before the commercial site opens</h2>
    <p>
      The operator's legal name and contact, providers, purposes, retention
      periods, request process and relevant transfer safeguards must be
      completed from real settings. Subscription and advertising integrations
      will receive a separate review before activation.
    </p>
    <h2>External links and downloads</h2>
    <p>
      Following a source link opens that provider's website under its practices.
      Downloaded CSVs contain public sample statistics and metadata, without
      personal account data.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
